3way-mpi - MPI Implementation
==============================
------------------------------
Running Manually (for testing)
------------------------------
1. Load Module:
    module load CMake/3.23.1-GCCcore-11.3.0 foss/2022a OpenMPI/4.1.4-GCC-11.3.0

2. compile with "make"

// Skeleton
    mpirun -np <num_processes> ./3way-mpi <input_file> [batch_size]

Example:
    mpirun -np 4 ./3way-mpi /homes/eyv/cis520/wiki_dump.txt

Optional batch_size argument controls how many lines are read at once.
When using run.sh, batch_size is set automatically based on --mem-per-cpu:
    64M  -> 2000 | 128M -> 5000 | 512M -> 20000 | other -> 50000

------------------------------
Scheduling on Beocat via Slurm
------------------------------
Edit run.sh to set your desired configuration:

    #SBATCH --nodes=<num_nodes>
    #SBATCH --ntasks-per-node=<cores_per_node>
    #SBATCH --mem-per-cpu=<memory>    (e.g. 1G, 512M, 64M)
    #SBATCH --time=<hh:mm:ss>

Submit a single job:

    sbatch run.sh

Submit multiple runs for statistical analysis:

    for i in $(seq 1 20); do sbatch run.sh; done

------------------------------
Output
------------------------------

All output goes to a single file per job:

- logs/mpi-%j.out   node config, timing, and stdout for each job

Node config and timing are printed to this file. Full program output
is suppressed by default (redirected to /dev/null). To capture full
output instead, swap the active/commented mpirun lines in run.sh.

